/-!
# Native five-simplex classes and their geometric relations

The original based five-simplex defines a native fifth homotopy class,
whose Hurewicz image is its actual corrected singular cycle.  The genuine
recursive five-cube chain is the signed sum of its 120 affine permutation
simplices.  Native recovery from these cells and the alternating relation
among the seven original faces of a based six-simplex use the existing
dimension-generic theorems, without repeating their geometric proofs.
-/
